  "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{e}^{2x-1}<-8{e}^{2x-1}-6x{e}^{2x-1} \\\\ {x}^{2}{e}^{2x-1}+6x{e}^{2x-1}+8{e}^{2x-1} & <0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+6x+8){e}^{2x-1} & <0 \\\\ (x+4)(x+2){e}^{2x-1} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${e}^{2x-1}$ and get\n\n$$\n(x+4)(x+2)<0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-4$ and $x=-2.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-4<x<-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/assets/15a31e60a938b604b96ade5e6868c658a2e2f0a53fe2a5f53a032093155e8aee.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-4<x<-2.$",
